{"chunk_id": "7437914a7d70", "text": "After Rama symbolically returns the golden sandals, Bharata vows to rule only as their custodian for the fourteen years of Rama\u2019s exile, living austerely and threatening self\u2011immolation if Rama does not return on the appointed day. Rama urges him to honor their mother Kaikeyi and protect the kingdom. In grief, the brothers part. Bharata reverently places the sandals upon the royal elephant and then on his own head before beginning the return from Chitrakuta with sages and counselors. He visits the hermitage of the sage Bharadwaja, recounts how Rama refused to break their father\u2019s command, and receives praise for his righteousness. Bharata then continues toward Ayodhya, his vast army crossing sacred rivers like the Yamuna and the Ganga.\nBharata accepts Rama\u2019s sandals as symbol of rule, vows austerity until Rama\u2019s return, then begins the journey back to Ayodhya.\nThemes: loyalty to dharma, symbolic kingship, brotherly devotion, renunciation and duty", "vector": [0.02433605119585991, -0.03649057075381279, -0.015085110440850258, -0.01320791244506836, -0.011526537127792835, 0.020878765732049942, -0.030926503241062164, -0.017178388312458992, -0.011445507407188416, -0.010804018005728722, 0.011337466537952423, 0.006857175379991531, 0.0074682775884866714, 0.020433099940419197, 0.007387247402220964, -0.013646826148033142, 0.040569089353084564, 0.002049387199804187, 0.04580903798341751, 0.00022283288126345724, -0.003727386239916086, -0.016948804259300232, -0.014477384276688099, 0.007745130453258753, -0.005483039189130068, -0.014801505021750927, 0.008906562812626362, -0.03322235494852066, 0.010149024426937103, -0.028819719329476357, -0.008285331539809704, -0.009831656701862812, -0.003518058452755213, 0.008643214590847492, -0.019474243745207787, 0.01145901158452034, -0.01081752311438322, 0.0034015777055174112, 0.02278297394514084, -0.013518528081476688, -0.0037003762554377317, 0.0004946214612573385, -0.0115197850391